# Frontend Standards

See `docs/11-frontend-architecture.md` and `docs/18-coding-standards.md`.

## Organization

- Feature-based directories under `apps/web`.
- Separate public, auth, user dashboard, and admin dashboard route groups.
- Reusable UI via shadcn/ui + project components; Lucide for icons.

## React / Next.js

- Prefer Server Components.
- Use Client Components only for interactivity, forms, charts, heartbeats, etc.
- TanStack Query for server state; avoid unnecessary global client stores.
- React Hook Form + Zod for forms; align schemas with `packages/shared` when possible.

## API & security UI

- Call the API only through typed client/services.
- Never treat UI hiding as authorization: premium answer/explanation UI must still assume the API omits restricted fields.
- Never put Cloudinary API secrets or unsigned unrestricted upload presets in client code.
- Do not store access tokens in `localStorage` if HTTP-only cookie strategy is selected; follow `docs/07-authentication-and-authorization.md`.

## UX boundaries

- Admin screens must be route-protected and still fail closed if the API returns 403.
- Post-trial users may browse questions; do not show fabricated “correct” markers client-side.
